{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1445023-trinity-continuum-character-creation-rulehack","id":1445023,"title":"[Trinity Continuum] Character Creation Rulehack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T04:59:07-07:00","id":1445023,"title":"[Trinity Continuum] Character Creation Rulehack","content":"As I will soon start my \u00c6ON game, I tweaked the character creation a bit.<br /> <br /> Instead of just 3 starting paths, the players get one additonal, by transforming the free dots in skills / edges into a path dot.<br /> They can either choose a secondary Role or Society path, or deepen an existing path. I also feel that it can help a character better in gamistic terms. It says a lot if a character has a stronger origin, role or society path, and thus maybe a main community or contact to go to, or i.e. a second role or society to show a divergent in occupation or conflicting loyalities.<br /> <br /> In game terms - Character creation:<br /> Choose one Origin, Role and Society Path at 1 dot each.<br /> Add 1 dot to any Path.<br /> Distribute 3 skills dots to any skills.<br /> Distribute 2 Edge dots to any Edges. You can also choose Skill Tricks instead of Edges.<br /> (As edges cost the same as skill tricks - i wanted to clearly include this. and i already had a player who asked about having more skill tricks.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2